<title>USA: Allegheny sees Q1 gain from Nitinol sale.</title>
<headline>Allegheny sees Q1 gain from Nitinol sale.</headline>
<dateline>PITTSBURGH 1997-03-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Allegheny Teledyne Inc on Monday said it would realize a first-quarter gain of $0.05 per share from the sale of its stake in Nitinol Development Corp to Johnson &amp; Johnson's Cordis Corp.</p>
<p>The company said it sold its interest in metal alloy business for $20 million. The first-quarter gain will amount to $9.2 million.</p>
<p>Allegheny Teledyne Inc is a group of technology-based manufacturing businesses concentrating in specialty metals, complemented by aerospace and electronics, industrial, and consumer products.</p>
</text>
